sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
CSS Grid is a two-dimensional layout system. A grid container can coordinate both columns and rows, which makes it a better fit than Flexbox when content needs alignment in two directions.

```css
main {
  display: grid;
}
```

**Line by line:** `main {` targets the existing semantic main region without changing the HTML. `display: grid;` creates the Grid formatting context so its direct children become grid items. The closing `}` ends that rule. The page structure stays exactly the same.

